    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's start with a number you already know.\n\n9 × 9 = 81.\n\nSo the square root of 81 is 9.\n\nSquare roots simply undo squaring.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A square root asks: what positive number multiplied by itself gives this number?\n\nFor 81, we ask what number makes 81 when squared.\n\n9 × 9 = 81, so √81 = 9.\n\nThe root sign is not another kind of division. It is undoing a square.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
