      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The chapter gives this useful rule:\n\n√(a × b) = √a × √b.\n\nUse it when a product contains easy square factors.\n\nExample: √(9 × 16) = 3 × 4 = 12.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
